tests/ui/hud-motion.ts:69-77:
```
const ctx = await context(browser, PHONE);
const page = await open(ctx, origin, STAGES_PAGE, STAGES_READY);
await page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion });
await page.evaluate((n) => { const w = window as unknown as { __stages: { render(n: string): void } }; w.__stages.render(n); }, `hud-motion--${name}`);
```
harness/screens/browser.ts:123 `renderStage(ctx, origin, name)` already does open + `__stages.render(n)` (+ `__settle()` + `document.fonts.ready`). tests/ui/keycap-legend-slide.test.ts:85-86 uses `renderStage(...)` and then `page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'reduce' })`. `__settle` finishes animations but does not change the computed `animation-name`/duration/delay that `probe` reads.
